    why: >
      Section 4.2's derived-not-stored discipline: standing/trust is COMPUTED on demand,
      never cached as a persisted number. VerificationMemo (memo.rs) deliberately carries
      depth: VerificationDepth (an enum) and epoch: TrustEpoch (an opaque token), never a
      bare numeric score — the module doc calls this out by name as the drift this rule
      exists to catch. If you are adding a `pub score: <number>`-shaped field anywhere in
      this seam, stop: the standing view (services::standing::Standing / StandingScore)
      is the ALREADY-DERIVED read model; nothing downstream should cache its own copy of
      a number that must always be recomputed from the live edge set.
  - id: stage-cannot-cheapen-the-floor
    class: ask
    when:
      write: "pricer.rs"
