      elohim/elohim-storage/src/trust/pricer.rs (module doc's THE safety invariant +
      every_in_crate_pricer_forces_full_chain_across_the_entire_product_space +
      conformance_harness_rejects_a_floor_cheapening_mutant +
      floor_forces_full_chain_even_at_simulacra)
    why: >
      THE safety keystone this program reviews before accepting any change here: a
      FloorClass other than None (Constitutional, LocalRelationship, CounterEvidence)
      forces VerificationDepth::FullChain at EVERY NetworkStage, including Simulacra —
      the "cheap dev/staging" stage is the one most tempted to cheapen it. Before landing
      a new VerificationPricer implementor or touching price()/FloorClass: (1) add the
      new implementor to tests::in_crate_pricers so the 4x4x8x6=768-case property test
      actually exercises it — an implementor absent from that registry is invisible to
      the keystone; (2) re-run
      every_in_crate_pricer_forces_full_chain_across_the_entire_product_space and
      conformance_harness_rejects_a_floor_cheapening_mutant and confirm both still pass.
      This is the strongest class this seam's rules carry (ask, not inject) because a
      silent floor-cheapening regression here is exactly the failure mode
      trust-as-efficiency-signal.md exists to prevent: trust must reduce verification
      cost, never eliminate it where a floor applies.
  - id: dev-mode-is-not-network-stage
    class: inject
    when: { write: "*.rs", contains-any: ["DEV_MODE", "dev_mode"] }
    dedupe-of: >
      elohim/elohim-storage/src/trust/stage.rs (module doc: NetworkStage must never
      derive from any DEV_MODE flag) + genesis/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-08-
      head-plane-trust-gradient-program-plan.md section 2 evidence correction #2
    why: >
      Two UNRELATED dev_modes already exist in this codebase: elohim-storage's
      (p2p/mod.rs) is inert (no supplier, no consumer); doorway's DEV_MODE (config.rs)
      is LIVE, auth-permissive, and true fleet-wide. NetworkStage must NEVER be derived
      from either — the durable home for declared stakes is the standing-policy manifest
      / ELOHIM_NETWORK_STAKES (T10), and unknown/absent resolves to
      NetworkStage::Bootstrap (fail-closed toward MORE scrutiny, never less). If you are
      reading a DEV_MODE/dev_mode flag anywhere in this seam to decide a stage, stop —
      that is precisely the conflation this plan corrected.
  - id: pure-half-stays-pure-stage
    class: inject
    when:
      write: "stage.rs"
      contains-any: ["diesel", "tokio", "SystemTime::now", "Instant::now", "chrono", "std::env", "env::var"]
    dedupe-of: "elohim/elohim-storage/src/trust/stage.rs (module doc: PURE module — no diesel, no tokio, no clock, no env)"
    why: >
      stage.rs is declared PURE — no diesel, no tokio, no clock, no env — so
      StakesResolver::stage_for stays testable with no conductor and so the eventual
      graduation to a standalone crates/trust-gradient (a git mv, per the module doc's
      C13 successor note) is a move, not a rewrite. A dependency on diesel/tokio/a wall
      clock/an env read belongs in a resolver's PRODUCTION implementation
      (ManifestStakesResolver, T10) constructed OUTSIDE this file and passed in as
      &dyn StakesResolver — never inlined here.
  - id: pure-half-stays-pure-pricer
    class: inject
    when:
      write: "pricer.rs"
      contains-any: ["diesel", "tokio", "SystemTime::now", "Instant::now", "chrono", "std::env", "env::var"]
    dedupe-of: "elohim/elohim-storage/src/trust/pricer.rs (module doc: PURE module — no diesel, no tokio, no clock, no env)"
    why: >
      Same discipline as stage.rs, for the pricing half: VerificationPricer::price must
      stay a pure PricingInput -> PricedVerification function so the floor property test
      (stage-cannot-cheapen-the-floor, this manifest) can exercise the full NetworkStage x
      FloorClass x Reach x Standing product with no conductor, no clock, and no I/O. A
      dependency on diesel/tokio/a wall clock/an env read belongs upstream, in whatever
      supplies PricingInput — never inside price() itself.
